  "rationale": "The batch shows a strong but overly broad period preference after nouns, while several observed continuations require a comma after the introductory “One morning,”, a paragraph break after a standalone opening phrase or a period, and an exclamation after “Until next time”. It also underweights the observed noun after “One” and “next”, and a conjunction after a proper noun. These additions favor those local, reusable constructions without treating them as mandatory in other contexts; punctuation and lexical alternatives remain possible elsewhere. The phrase-specific rules are supported by this single revealed document and may be too narrow or overconfident in other stories. Replay behavior has not been evaluated."
